<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="palabras-ws-espanglishemos">
<title>ESPaNgliSHemos</title>


<page>
<exercise xml:id="ex-translate-1">
  <statement>
    <p>Translate these words to Spanish/English. For the last 2, pick any words! 
    <ul>
      <li> Write their <term>length</term> (# of letters).</li> 
      <li>In each case, find the scaling factor going from English to Spanish.</li>
    </ul>
    </p>
    <sbsgroup widths="47% 47%" margins="0% 0%" valign="bottom">
      <sidebyside>
        <image source="espanglishemos-leche-milk.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <image source="espanglishemos-ballena-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
      </sidebyside>

      <sidebyside>
        <image source="espanglishemos-house-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <image source="espanglishemos-pig-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
      </sidebyside>

      <sidebyside>
        <image source="espanglishemos-raton-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <image source="espanglishemos-corazon-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
      </sidebyside>

      <sidebyside>
        <image source="espanglishemos-door-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <image source="espanglishemos-avocado-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>  
    </sidebyside>

      <sidebyside>
        <image source="espanglishemos-zanahoria-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <image source="espanglishemos-empty-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>  
      </sidebyside>

      <sidebyside>
        <image source="espanglishemos-strawberry-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>
        <image source="espanglishemos-empty-empty.png">
          <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
        </image>  
      </sidebyside>
    </sbsgroup>
  </statement>

  <solution>

<p>We illustrate in detail the case of the pair <q>DOOR</q>, <q>PUERTA</q>. The scaling factors are 1.5 and 0.66 (periodic). These are different ways to find them: </p>
            <image source="espanglishemos-door-puerta.png" width="60%">
              <shortdescription></shortdescription>
            </image>
            <paragraphs>
              <title>From English to Spanish</title> 
              <image source="espanglishemos-exampleEngToSpa.png" width="30%">
                <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
              </image>
              <p>The length increased, so the scaling factor is <m>\gt 1</m>.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><p>One way: think<ellipsis/> which number I can multiply 4 by to get 6? Solution: <alert>1.5</alert>.</p></li>
                <li><p>Another way: divide by 4 (to get 1), then multiply by 6 (to get 6). This is the same as multiplying (in a single step) by <m>6/4</m>.</p></li>
                <li><p>Another way: divide by 2 (to get 2), then multiply by 3 (to get 6). This is the same as multiplying (in a single step) by <m>3/2</m>.</p></li>
                <li><p>Another way: look at the tape diagram and see that the length grows by half, so this is a <alert>+50%</alert> growth. (or: a scaling of <alert>150%</alert>)</p></li>
              </ul>
            </paragraphs>
            <paragraphs>
              <title>From Spanish to English</title>
              <image source="espanglishemos-exampleSpaToEng.png" width="30%">
                <shortdescription>(for accessibility)</shortdescription>
              </image>
              <p>The length decreased, so the scaling factor is <m>\lt 1</m>.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><p>One way: think<ellipsis/> which number I can multiply 6 by to get 4? Solution: <m>2/3</m>, since 4 is two thirds of 6.</p></li>
                <li><p>Another way: divide by 6 (to get 1), then multiply by 4 (to get 4). This is the same as multiplying (in a single step) by <m>4/6</m>.</p></li>
                <li><p>Another way: divide by 3 (to get 2), then multiply by 2 (to get 4). This is the same as multiplying (in a single step) by <m>2/3</m>.</p></li>
                <li><p>Another way: look at the tape diagram and see that the length gets cut by 1/3, so this is a change of <alert>−33.3%</alert> (or a 33.3% decrease, or a scaling of 66.66%).</p></li>
                <li><p>Another way: since 1.5 was the scaling factor going from ENG to SPA, the reverse should be <m>1/(1.5) = (1/1)/(3/2) = 2/3</m>.</p></li>
              </ul>
            </paragraphs>
    <p>
      The following table summarizes the lengths of the words, and the scaling factors going from English to Spanish.
    </p>
    <tabular>
      <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
        <cell>English</cell><cell>length</cell><cell>Spanish</cell><cell>length</cell><cell>ENG→SPA</cell>
      </row>
      <row><cell>MILK</cell><cell>4</cell><cell>LECHE</cell><cell>5</cell><cell><m>5/4 = 1.25</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>WHALE</cell><cell>5</cell><cell>BALLENA</cell><cell>7</cell><cell><m>7/5 = 1.4</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>HOUSE</cell><cell>5</cell><cell>CASA</cell><cell>4</cell><cell><m>4/5 = 0.8</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>PIG</cell><cell>3</cell><cell>CERDO</cell><cell>5</cell><cell><m>5/3 \approx 1.66</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>MOUSE</cell><cell>5</cell><cell>RATÓN</cell><cell>5</cell><cell><m>5/5 = 1</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>HEART</cell><cell>5</cell><cell>CORAZÓN</cell><cell>7</cell><cell><m>7/5 = 1.4</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>DOOR</cell><cell>4</cell><cell>PUERTA</cell><cell>6</cell><cell><m>6/4 = 1.5</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>AVOCADO</cell><cell>7</cell><cell>AGUACATE</cell><cell>8</cell><cell><m>8/7 \approx 1.14</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>CARROT</cell><cell>6</cell><cell>ZANAHORIA</cell><cell>9</cell><cell><m>9/6 = 1.5</m></cell></row>
      <row><cell>STRAWBERRY</cell><cell>10</cell><cell>FRESA</cell><cell>5</cell><cell><m>5/10 = 0.5</m></cell></row>
    </tabular>
  </solution>
</exercise>
</page>

<page>

<exercise xml:id="ex-translate-2">
  <statement>
    <p>Now complete this table. It has the lengths of words, and scaling factor and percentage of increase/decrease going from English to Spanish.</p>

      <tabular halign="center" rowstretch="1.5">
          <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
            <cell>English</cell><cell>length</cell><cell>Spanish</cell><cell>length</cell><cell>Scaling Factor</cell><cell>% of inc./dec.</cell>
          </row>
